Little XM Tracker on Mortar. Every change is behind MORTAR_BUILD (set by
pkgs/little-xm-tracker); other builds are unchanged.

- TrackerApp.cpp, controller(): the app names buttons after the Brick's
  printed labels and upstream relies on KNULLI's patched SDL mapping for
  that. Here SDL auto-maps the evdev pad (A = BTN_EAST = SDL "B", B =
  BTN_SOUTH = SDL "A"), so swap them, and in the --ui-test fixture too.
- TrackerApp.cpp, run(): glyphs are drawn one fill rect per pixel and the
  whole screen is redrawn every frame. With no input for 500 ms, nothing
  playing and no worker busy, redraw at 10 fps (still polling events).

diff --git a/src/ui/TrackerApp.cpp b/src/ui/TrackerApp.cpp
index f48f066..63db6ee 100644
